Tell ld64 which platform the kernels are linked for

pocl links each compiled kernel through lld's library API, and builds the
argument list for ld64 with -arch but no -platform_version. ld64 refuses a
link that does not name the platform, so on macOS the in-process link
failed for every kernel -- twice per specialisation -- and pocl fell back
to spawning the Clang driver, which is the slow path this function exists
to avoid. The rendering was correct, but each kernel paid for a failed
link first and the errors reached the application's stderr.

The versions come from the triplet the kernels were compiled for, which is
the one they have to be linked for.
diff --git a/lib/CL/pocl_llvm_build.cc b/lib/CL/pocl_llvm_build.cc
index 97b4889d..a77ee6a5 100644
--- a/lib/CL/pocl_llvm_build.cc
+++ b/lib/CL/pocl_llvm_build.cc
@@ -1231,10 +1231,19 @@ int pocl_invoke_lld_link(cl_device_id Device, const char *InFile,
   // Symbols the kernel binary leaves undefined resolve when it is
   // dlopen()ed, so no C runtime or startup files are needed at link time.
 #ifdef __APPLE__
-  ArgStorage.push_back(
-      llvm::Triple(Device->llvm_target_triplet).getArchName().str());
+  llvm::Triple TargetTriple(Device->llvm_target_triplet);
+  ArgStorage.push_back(TargetTriple.getArchName().str());
+  /* ld64 rejects a link that does not name the platform and its versions,
+     so without this every kernel fails here and falls back to the Clang
+     driver -- the slow path this function exists to avoid. The triplet is
+     what the kernels were compiled for, so it is also what to link them
+     for; a triplet carrying no version leaves an empty string, which ld64
+     reports just as it would a missing one. */
+  ArgStorage.push_back(TargetTriple.getOSVersion().getAsString());
   LinkerArgs = {"ld64.lld", "-dylib", "-undefined", "dynamic_lookup",
-                "-arch",    ArgStorage[0].c_str(), "-o", OutFile,
+                "-arch",    ArgStorage[0].c_str(),
+                "-platform_version", "macos", ArgStorage[1].c_str(),
+                ArgStorage[1].c_str(), "-o", OutFile,
                 InFile};
   Drivers = {{lld::Darwin, &lld::macho::link}};
 #else
